  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "granja-sotano",
      "id": "LUG-02",
      "plano": "granja-sotano",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.NNzMhIvsavpG0iTQ]{The Sheriff's Farm and Boat Landing}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.doItxeK8y7M1PufU.JournalEntryPage.ogKpm1VYgcVGCw1T]{A4-E02 · The Raid}</p>\n<p><strong>The farm cellar.</strong> Under the house (same footprint as the ground floor, shifted +0,5 m in x and −1 m in y). Old flagstone floor, shelves of preserves, the furnace, a chest freezer, and the steel gun locker. You get down by the stairs in the hall (region “Up to the house” / “Arrival”).</p>\n<p><strong>The Sheriff&#39;s chamber.</strong> Dirt floor, an iron cot: Montgomery sleeps here by day. Heavy door.</p>\n<p><strong>The tunnel to the boat landing.</strong> Behind the <strong>preserves shelf</strong> on the north wall (tile: it slides like a door) is a <strong>hidden door</strong> (wall with door=2: it looks like a wall) to the roughly <strong>300 m</strong> tunnel that comes out at the private boat landing on the Snohomish River. In A4-E02, “through the farm: the tunnel to the river boat landing. The dogs cover the retreat.” Montgomery and Hal know about it; the rest only if someone shows them. The tunnel region has no destination: the boat landing is on the zone map (t2i).</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (2) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> Tunnel to the river boat landing (300 m).</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
